# Normalize line endings — this repo is built and run in LINUX containers.
#
# Why: on Windows, `core.autocrlf=true` (the default) converts LF to CRLF on
# checkout. The shell scripts are MOUNTED into containers and executed by the
# container's Linux bash — with CRLF the shebang line becomes
# `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r`, bash reports "command not found" and the init
# container exits 127:
#
#     service "kafka-topics" didn't complete successfully: exit 127
#
# `eol=lf` makes git write LF in the working tree on EVERY platform, and
# `text=auto` normalizes the index to LF, so the repo stays byte-identical
# everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Scripts are executed, not read — they MUST be LF.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.conf text eol=lf

# Binary-ish assets: never touch the line endings.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
